**Proposed source interface for `mount` / `push` to dispatch on.** It comes from #1960 (bean `l4ay`), following the owner's ruling of 2026-10-03: *"A sub graph declares where it's getting its content … That same information can be overwritten by the harness instance config."* This PR's files are untouched. Nothing in #1960 edits `branch-store.ts`, `special-branches.json` or #1937's schema.

### What a declaration can say (`cat-harness/schemas/subgraph-source.ts`)
```ts
// on a directories[] entry; absent = { kind: "directory" }
source?: { kind: "directory" }
       | { kind: "branch"; branch: string /* plain name, declared in special-branches.json */; keyedBy: "commit" | "tip" }
// <instance>.config.json, matched on directory id (never path); the checkout root's config wins
subgraphSources?: Record<dirId, SubgraphSource>
```
`storage: { branch, keyedBy }` (#1764 / #1937) maps exactly onto `source: { kind: "branch", branch, keyedBy }`. The resolver reads either one. It refuses an entry that carries both, and it refuses a `qa` subgraph keyed by `tip`.

### The one resolver (`cat-harness/schemas/harness-config.ts`)
```ts
declaredSubgraph(start: string, id: string): DeclaredSubgraph | undefined   // throws on a contradiction
interface DeclaredSubgraph { id; instanceRoot; instanceName; repository?; entry: ResolvedDirectory; source: ResolvedSubgraphSource }
type ResolvedSubgraphSource =
  | { kind: "directory"; id; path; declaredIn }
  | { kind: "branch"; id; path /* mount point */; branch; keyedBy;
      special: { id; shape; name; legacy: string[] } | undefined;   // the special-branches.json row, exact or family
      declaredIn }
// declaredIn: "default" | "declaration" | "storage" | "config"
```
Precedence: config override, then `source`, then `storage`, then `directory`. `SUBGRAPH_SOURCE_KINDS` lists the kinds the union knows.

### Dispatch as you described it
```ts
const d = declaredSubgraph(root, id);            // undefined → "no such subgraph" (exit 1)
switch (d.source.kind) {
  case "directory": /* mount: the checkout path IS the content, a no-op; push: "commit through git", no-op */ break;
  case "branch":
    if (d.source.keyedBy !== "tip") /* refuse: commit-keyed belongs to qa-store */;
    if (!d.source.special) /* refuse: branch not declared */;
    // resolveTipLocation becomes this case: name = special.name, with legacy fallback via special.legacy; into = d.source.path
    break;
  default: /* refuse unknown kind with its own exit code — never read it as a directory */
}
```
A TypeScript `switch` on `kind` turns a future kind such as `graph-db` into a compile error at your call site. The executable picture is `cat-harness/processes/kg/mount-subgraph.bpmn`. The shell view is `bun run subgraph:resolve <id> [--json] | --all`.

**Order:** #1960 targets `main` and doesn't depend on #1937. The `storage` mapping means either one can land first.

